>From when I first started playing NetHack, Ability Scores frustrated
me. Contrary to our RPG-honed stereotypes, Rangers had low dexterity,
Wizards had low wisdom, and melee fighters had high dexterity.

I know that ability scores don't make a huge difference, but as I
understand it, NetHack's additions are loosely based on Dungeons and
Dragons, so why not implement some of the balancing elements that D&D
has?

My YANIs:

Use D&D's interactive stat-rolling element, whether this means point
buy, one-chance, 6 retries, or what, and furthermore, let us swap our
rolled scores around. The fact that Intelligence and Charisma cannot
be exercized can hurt in the early game.

Use D&D's unarmed/melee/missile system: That is, melee strikes' to hit
are modified by Str, and ranged weapons are modified by Dex. An item
or intrinsic mimicking the feat Weapon Finesse could be added, and you
probably know that in D&D, heavy ranged weapons can have Str penalties
applied.

Maybe, just maybe, enable all races as all classes, and introduce
racial stat modifiers.



